{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And there arose a new king.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory disagree concerning this: some of them say he was literally new, and some say that his decrees were renewed. And it appears to explain that this king was born at the time when Joseph was in the prison — this is what is written concerning him (Genesis 40:20): ״יום הולדת את פרעה״, that is, the day on which Pharaoh was born — for the king called his son by his own name; and this accords with the words of the one who says 'literally new.' And this is what it says: 'who did not know Joseph' — for he did not know him nor recognize him at all, because he was the son of the first, old king." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'Who did not know Joseph' — whoever denies the kindness done by his fellow, in the end he will deny the kindness of the Holy One, blessed be He, for it is written: 'who did not know Joseph,' and in the end he said (Exodus 5): ״לא ידעתי את ה׳״. To what may the matter be likened? To a man who stoned the icon of the duke. The king said: 'Cut off his head.' Tomorrow he will do the same to me. And this Midrash inclines toward the one who says his decrees were renewed."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:08.548978747Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}